{"id":"653f289b6af2e4be","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-gelfand-graev.md","title":"Gelfand–Graev Character","display":"thm-gelfand-graev — Gelfand–Graev Character","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-gelfand-graev","aliases":["58-thm-gelfand-graev"],"display":"thm-gelfand-graev — Gelfand–Graev Character","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-gelfand-graev"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-gelfand-graev</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-gelfand-graev — Gelfand–Graev Character"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-group.md\">../batch09/58-df-group.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md\">../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G,U,\\cdot_G,\\psi,\\chi\\in V\">\\(G,U,\\cdot_G,\\psi,\\chi\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Group}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Group}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|\">\\(|\\cdot|\\)</span> are the imported predicates and cardinality operator</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x^{-1}\">\\(x^{-1}\\)</span> denotes the inverse determined by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot_G)\">\\(\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot_G)\\)</span></li>\n<li>In the Gelfand--Graev specialization, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span> is a finite reductive group, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> is a maximal unipotent subgroup, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\psi\">\\(\\psi\\)</span> is nondegenerate; the displayed theorem uses only the group-theoretic data needed for the induced-character formula</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}gelfand\\text{-}graev}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(G)\n\\land U\\subseteq G\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_S(U,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(U\\times U))\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\psi,U,\\mathbb C^\\times)\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in U\\;\\bigl(\\psi(u\\cdot_Gv)=\\psi(u)\\psi(v)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists\\chi\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(\\chi,G,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\forall g\\in G\\;\n\\chi(g)=\\frac1{|U|}\n\\sum_{\\substack{x\\in G\\\\x^{-1}\\cdot_Gg\\cdot_Gx\\in U}}\n\\psi(x^{-1}\\cdot_Gg\\cdot_Gx)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}gelfand\\text{-}graev}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(G)\n\\land U\\subseteq G\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_S(U,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(U\\times U))\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\psi,U,\\mathbb C^\\times)\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in U\\;\\bigl(\\psi(u\\cdot_Gv)=\\psi(u)\\psi(v)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists\\chi\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(\\chi,G,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\forall g\\in G\\;\n\\chi(g)=\\frac1{|U|}\n\\sum_{\\substack{x\\in G\\\\x^{-1}\\cdot_Gg\\cdot_Gx\\in U}}\n\\psi(x^{-1}\\cdot_Gg\\cdot_Gx)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The formula is the ordinary induced-character formula for the\nGelfand--Graev representation.  The former assertion incorrectly claimed\nthat every character was a Fourier transform of an orbital integral and\ndepended on unrelated Gelfand-transform and Dirichlet-character atoms.</li>\n<li>The unsupported predicates for finite groups, maximal unipotence, trace characters, and nondegeneracy have been removed from the formal core.  For maximal unipotent <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> and nondegenerate <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\psi\">\\(\\psi\\)</span>, the resulting induced character is precisely the Gelfand--Graev character.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed71f39f59370734","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-finite.md","status":"resolved","id":"d9a25b0ac94a3598","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"G,U,\\cdot_G,\\psi,\\chi\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Group}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Finite}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"|\\cdot|","display":false},{"tex":"x^{-1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot_G)","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"\\psi","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}gelfand\\text{-}graev}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(G)\n\\land U\\subseteq G\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_S(U,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(U\\times U))\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\psi,U,\\mathbb C^\\times)\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in U\\;\\bigl(\\psi(u\\cdot_Gv)=\\psi(u)\\psi(v)\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\\exists\\chi\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(\\chi,G,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\forall g\\in G\\;\n\\chi(g)=\\frac1{|U|}\n\\sum_{\\substack{x\\in G\\\\x^{-1}\\cdot_Gg\\cdot_Gx\\in U}}\n\\psi(x^{-1}\\cdot_Gg\\cdot_Gx)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"\\psi","display":false}],"bytes":2032,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4173","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-gelfand-graev.md|58-thm-gelfand-graev]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["ed71f39f59370734","d9a25b0ac94a3598","36d7463d215be751","2be08d4ee8aa1590"]}